# Tailwind CSS v4 Rewrite Examples

Apply these patterns when updating or generating frontend code in matching files.

## Prefer v4 setup

```css
/* BAD v3 style */
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;

/* GOOD v4 style */
@import "tailwindcss";
```

```js
// BAD v3-era plugin setup
export default { plugins: { tailwindcss: {}, autoprefixer: {} } };

// GOOD v4 PostCSS setup
export default { plugins: ["@tailwindcss/postcss"] };
```

## Prefer CSS-first customization

```css
/* GOOD v4 theme tokens in CSS */
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  --color-brand-500: oklch(0.62 0.18 264);
  --font-display: "Inter", sans-serif;
  --breakpoint-3xl: 120rem;
}
```

## Prefer v4-native utilities and variants

```html
<!-- GOOD container queries from core -->
<section class="@container">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 @sm:grid-cols-2 @lg:grid-cols-4"></div>
</section>
```

```html
<!-- GOOD modern gradients -->
<div class="bg-linear-45 from-indigo-500 via-purple-500 to-pink-500"></div>
```

```html
<!-- GOOD dynamic values and data variants -->
<div data-current class="grid grid-cols-15 data-current:opacity-100"></div>
```

```html
<!-- GOOD newer variants -->
<button class="not-hover:opacity-80 starting:open:opacity-0 inert:opacity-50"></button>
```

## Migration behavior rules

- Do not add `content` config by default in v4 migrations; trust automatic detection.
- If classes are in excluded sources, add `@source` in CSS instead of broad scanning config.
- Convert only what is needed for parity; preserve behavior first.
- If code appears mixed between v3 and v4 and intent is unclear, ask before sweeping rewrites.
